    "raw_response": "```json\n{\n  \"inputs\": [\n    \"internalTime\",\n    \"TAmb\",\n    \"TDif\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"outputs[1]\",\n    \"outputs[2]\",\n    \"heatCapacitor.T\",\n    \"heatingResistor.heatPort.Q_flow\",\n    \"onOffController.y\"\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"This scenario investigates the behavior of a controlled temperature system using step, ramp, and sine excitations. The 'internalTime' is used as the simulation clock, 'TAmb' is set to a constant ambient temperature, and 'TDif' represents the error in temperature. A step input is applied to the heating resistor's heat flow to simulate an initial change in power. A ramp input is applied to 'internalTime' to gradually increase the system's time, simulating a change in the thermal dynamics over time. Finally, a sine wave is applied to 'TAmb' to mimic periodic changes in ambient temperature. The outputs are tracked to observe system temperature dynamics, heating power, and controller states.\"\n}\n```"
